This is anthra_conf. anthra_conf is a small tool to make tomsax's wunderfull and 
distinguished anthra_1920_FSE a little bit more configurable, while beeing 
itself highly configurable.

anthra_conf is intended to add or change strings in a template file and insert 
the changed templates in the skin file. A sample/default configuration is provided,
which adds menuicons and submenuicons to the skinfile.


INSTALLATION:

The directory anthra_conf has to be in the anthra directory.

To make anthra-conf to be a little more verbose, you can uncomment the DEBUG
variable - to make it fully verbose you can uncomment "set -x".

Customize or extend the configurationfiles to suit your needs:

mainmenu_menuorg.conf: mainmenuentries generated by menuorg
mainmenu_plugins.conf: mainmenuentries generated by plugins
mainmenu_trans.conf: translated mainmenuentries, new entries need new translations!  
mainmenu_yavdr_menuorg: only for yaVDR-menu, don't forget to set 'yaVDR = 1' in anthras Make.config

submenu_plugins.conf: for plugins with own setup
submenu_trans.conf: see mainmenu_trans.conf above
submenu_vdrsetup.conf: VDRs own setup

Syntax ist Simple:
The *.confs are divided in two columns, separator is ":"

exact MenuString:PictureName

A '#' at the beginning of a line makes anthra_conf to ignore the line. 
PictureName is given without extension and had to be in the MAINMENULOGO- or
SUBMENULOGO-DIR of anthra.
In anthra_confs newmainmenulogos-dir are some new logos. If you want use them
move them to anrhras MAINMENULOGO-DIR 

Spaces and umlauts (yes, if've checked this in my dictionary) are welcome in the
menuname-column but Do NOT use ':'. 

As PictureName you must take one of the logos in anthras mainmenulogos-dir or
one of new logos in anthra_confs newmainmenulogos-dir. If you use newmainmenulogos
move them to anthras mainmenulogos-dir!

After editing *.confs, go to the anthra-dir (one step up) and call 'make clean all'.
If the skinfile is generated well, call 'make install'.

CONFIGURATION for the hardboiled


You con add your own config-triples existing of
1. <string>.conf
2. templates/<string>.tmpl
3. <!--<STRING>-INSPT--> in 03_menu.xml (Important: UPPERCASE) 

anthra_conf insert its generated code before! lines containing 
<!--<STRING>-INSPT-->.

The files in the templates subdirectory may also be suspects to an open hearted
xml-understander: each line will be subtituted with the values from menuiconsmap.conf
submenuiconsmap.conf and finally put in the skinfile. Keywords had to be MENUSTRING
and PICSTRING. Even if you have decided to substitued something diffrent from picture
names.

Have fun!
